495
00:50:53,486 --> 00:50:56,132
Introduction to descriptive statistics.

496
00:50:56,558 --> 00:50:58,096
Descriptive statistics.

497
00:50:58,414 --> 00:51:05,700
A descriptive measurement is summary measure that quantitatively portrays the most important features of a set of data.

498
00:51:06,286 --> 00:51:11,876
Allowing for a better comprehension of the information, data can be measured as different levels.

499
00:51:12,366 --> 00:51:18,340
The levels of measurement describe the nature of information stored in the data assigned to the variables.

500
00:51:18,798 --> 00:51:22,416
Qualitative data can be measured as nominal or ordinal.

501
00:51:22,670 --> 00:51:27,216
Quantitative data can be measured in terms of interval and ratio type.

502
00:51:27,502 --> 00:51:28,496
Nominal data.

503
00:51:28,718 --> 00:51:32,736
The data is categorized using names, labels, or qualities.

504
00:51:33,006 --> 00:51:36,228
For example, brand name, zip code, and gender.

505
00:51:36,558 --> 00:51:41,296
