555
00:56:05,774 --> 00:56:11,300
Like in this case, 7 has the highest frequency, hence 7 becomes the mode value.

556
00:56:11,790 --> 00:56:19,140
However, in case of continuous data or quantitative data, the calculation of mode is slightly different.

557
00:56:19,694 --> 00:56:30,244
The first step in calculation of mode is dividing the data into classes which are equal with, then getting the frequency of data points lying in within that range of classes,

558
00:56:30,734 --> 00:56:34,180
and finally selecting the class with the highest frequency.

559
00:56:36,142 --> 00:56:41,156
Using the range of that class and the frequencies, we can get the final mode value.

