588
00:59:44,270 --> 00:59:48,612
The difference between the three distinct curves can be studied in this image.

589
00:59:49,646 --> 00:59:53,060
The central curve is the normal or no skewness curve.

590
00:59:53,390 --> 00:59:57,124
Here mean, median, and mode all lie on the same point.

591
00:59:57,646 --> 01:00:02,084
This normal curve is symmetrical about its mean, median, and mode.

592
01:00:04,526 --> 01:00:09,988
That means the left hand side of the curve is a mirror image of the right hand side of the curve.

593
01:00:11,758 --> 01:00:15,140
However, in case of negatively skewed data,

594
01:00:16,046 --> 01:00:18,852
the tail is elongated on the left hand side,

595
01:00:20,014 --> 01:00:26,596
and the mean is smaller than the mode and the median values, or is on the left hand side of the mode,

596
01:00:28,494 --> 01:00:32,292
hence indicating that the outliers are in the negative direction.

597
01:00:33,262 --> 01:00:40,388
On the other hand, in case of positively skewed the data, is concentrated on the left hand side of the curve,

598
01:00:42,190 --> 01:00:46,404
while the tail is elongated or longer on the right hand side of the curve.

599
01:00:48,078 --> 01:00:50,724
The mean is greater than the mode and median,

600
01:00:51,726 --> 01:00:58,180
or is on the right hand side of the mode and median indicating that the outliers are in the positive direction.

601
