01:17:06,062 --> 01:17:08,772
Let's say we have a data on a per year basis.

769
01:17:09,166 --> 01:17:17,444
So again, we can have a more skewness towards the right side, where data is being dropping as we continue to increase the number of years.

770
01:17:18,030 --> 01:17:24,272
For example, we may have a high sales towards the beginning of year, suppose in 2022.

771
01:17:24,782 --> 01:17:30,852
But again, as we proceed to 2023, second half we are seeing the dip in performance.

772
01:17:31,406 --> 01:17:33,072
So that is rightly skewed.

