01:17:47,790 --> 01:17:52,164
So it's more like skew towards the left section as a part of negative skew.

776
01:17:52,750 --> 01:17:54,660
Next we have kurtosis.

777
01:17:56,398 --> 01:18:01,316
So kurtosis is basically a measure of the tailedness of a distribution.

778
01:18:02,670 --> 01:18:07,472
So tailedness is how often the outliers occur and acts as kurtosis.

779
01:18:07,712 --> 01:18:12,132
Is the tailedness of the distribution related to a normal distribution?

780
01:18:12,750 --> 01:18:20,388
So a distribution with medium kurtosis is called as mesocurtic, a distribution with low kurtosis like this one.

781
01:18:20,846 --> 01:18:26,084
This is called as the platycurtic and then distribution with high kurtosis like this one.

782
01:18:26,414 --> 01:18:28,644
This is called as the leptocurtic.

783
01:18:30,126 --> 01:18:35,012
So tails here they are tapering ends on either side of a distribution like this.

784
01:18:35,470 --> 01:18:42,500
So they represent the probability or the frequency of values that are extremely high or extremely low to the mean.

785
01:18:43,822 --> 01:18:48,324
In other words, tails here represents how often the outliers occur.

786
01:18:50,062 --> 01:18:52,228
So there are three types of kurtosis.

787
01:18:52,846 --> 01:19:02,756
We have platycurtic, which is negative, leptocurtic, which is a positive towards the upper end, and then we have mesocurtic, which is a normal distribution.

788
01:19:03,182 --> 01:19:09,124
So mesocurtic is the medium tail, so normal distributions they have a kurtosis of three.

789
01:19:09,552 --> 01:19:19,748
So any distribution with a kurtosis of a prox value of three is going to be mesocurtic, and kurtosis is described in terms of excess kurtosis,

790
01:19:20,046 --> 01:19:22,308
which is kurtosis minus three.

791
01:19:22,798 --> 01:19:33,124
And since normal distribution, they have a kurtosis of three axis kurtosis makes comparing a distribution kurtosis to a normal distribution even easier.

