01:19:33,742 --> 01:19:35,524
Introduction to probability.

793
01:19:37,422 --> 01:19:38,788
Probability theory.

794
01:19:39,438 --> 01:19:43,524
Probability is a measure of the likelihood that an event will occur.

795
01:19:45,614 --> 01:19:48,132
Let's consider an example of coin toss,

796
01:19:49,070 --> 01:19:53,472
where the chances of getting heads on a coin are 1 by 2 or 50%.

797
01:19:55,502 --> 01:20:00,644
The probability of each given event is between 0 and 1, both inclusive.

798
01:20:01,294 --> 01:20:05,988
Sum of an event's cumulative probability cannot be greater than 1.

799
01:20:07,758 --> 01:20:12,132
Hence the probability of an event x lies between 0 and 1.

800
01:20:12,686 --> 01:20:18,340
This means that the integral of probability of distribution over x equals to 1.

801
01:20:21,006 --> 01:20:22,500
Conditional probability.

802
01:20:22,958 --> 01:20:29,348
Conditional probability of any event A is defined as the probability of occurrence of A,

803
01:20:29,998 --> 01:20:32,964
given that event B has previously occurred.

804
01:20:35,214 --> 01:20:43,072
Condition probability of event A given B can be estimated as probability of A intersection B, that is

805
01:20:43,312 --> 01:20:46,788
probability of both A and B happening together,

806
01:20:47,598 --> 01:20:49,860
divided by the probability of B.

807
01:20:52,558 --> 01:21:03,172
It is also written as that probability of A intersection B equals to probability of A given B multiplied to probability of B.

808
01:21:05,934 --> 01:21:07,524
Let's consider an example.

809
01:21:08,750 --> 01:21:11,392
