16:31:55,630 --> 16:32:04,400
What is data normalization and why do we need it? This is so important. We spend so much time in normalizing our data and getting our data clean and setting it up.

11662
16:32:04,720 --> 16:32:09,040
So we talk about data, there's a pre-processing step to standardize the data.

11663
16:32:09,200 --> 16:32:18,640
So whatever we have coming in, we don't want it to be a one gigabyte file here, a two gigabyte picture here, and a three-kilobyte text there.

11664
16:32:18,800 --> 16:32:26,240
Even as a human, I can't process those all in the same group. I have to reformat them in some way that loops them together so that the standardized format.

11665
16:32:26,400 --> 16:32:33,360
We use this data normalization in pre-processing to reduce it and eliminate data redundancy.

11666
16:32:33,600 --> 16:32:40,720
A lot of times the data comes in and you end up with two of the same images or the same information in different formats.

11667
16:32:40,880 --> 16:32:50,400
Then we want to rescale values to fit into a particular range for achieving better convergence. What this means is with most neural networks they form a bias.

11668
16:32:50,640 --> 16:32:58,960
We've seen this in recently in attacks on neural networks where they light up one pixel or one piece of the view and it skews the whole answer.

11669
16:32:59,120 --> 16:33:04,000
So suddenly because one pixel is really bright, it doesn't know what to do.

11670
16:33:04,160 --> 16:33:12,800
Well, when we start rescaling it, we put all the values between say minus one and one, and we change them and refit them to those values, it helps get rid of that bias,

11671
16:33:12,960 --> 16:33:22,160
helps fix for some of those problems. And then finally we restructure the data and improve the integrity. We want to make sure that we're not missing values or we don't have partial data coming in.

11672
16:33:22,400 --> 16:33:30,080
One way to look at this is bad data in, bad data out. So we want clean data in and you want good answers coming out.

