16:41:59,408 --> 16:42:02,928
It will change the weight going to each of the one of those nodes in the hidden layer.

11741
16:42:03,008 --> 16:42:12,528
And then based upon the error that's still being carried back, it'll change the weights going to the next hidden layer. And then it computes an error level on that and sends that back up.

11742
16:42:12,608 --> 16:42:17,808
And you're going to say, well, if it computes the error into the first hidden layer and fixes it, why would it stop there?

11743
16:42:17,968 --> 16:42:28,768
Well, remember, we don't want to create a biased neural network. So we only make small adjustments on these weights. We don't make a big adjustment that changes everything right off the bat.

11744
16:42:28,928 --> 16:42:35,168
So no matter how far back you go, you're always going to have a small amount of error, and that's still going to continue to go all the way back up the hidden layers.

11745
16:42:35,408 --> 16:42:46,768
For right now, focus on the back propagation is taking that error and moving it backwards on the neural network to change the weights and help program it so that it'll have the correct answers.

