And then finally, it's not sensitive to irrelevant features.

14202
20:49:48,832 --> 20:49:55,872
So it picks up on your different probabilities, and if you're short on data on one probability, you can kind of it automatically adjust for that.

14203
20:49:56,014 --> 20:50:05,232
Those formulas are very automatic, and so you can still get a very solid predictability, even if you're missing data or you have overlapping data for two completely different areas.

14204
20:50:05,392 --> 20:50:15,632
We see that a lot in doing census and studying of people and habits, where they might have one study that covers one aspect, another one that overlaps, and because the two overlap,

14205
20:50:15,872 --> 20:50:21,152
they can then predict the unknowns for the group that they haven't done the second study on, or vice versa.

14206
20:50:21,312 --> 20:50:29,392
So it's very powerful in that it is not sensitive to the irrelevant features, and in fact, you can use it to help predict features that aren't even in there.

