So you need to tell the system how many clusters we need to perform.

14915
22:01:40,398 --> 22:01:47,600
So if k is equal to two, there will be two clusters, if k is equal to three, three clusters, and so on and so forth. That's what the k stands for.

14916
22:01:47,854 --> 22:01:54,820
And of course, there is a way of finding out what is the best or optimum value of k for a given data. We will look at that.

14917
22:01:55,040 --> 22:01:57,476
So that is k means clustering.

