15596
23:17:13,856 --> 23:17:15,908
Now coming to the sixth question,

15597
23:17:17,262 --> 23:17:21,668
what are the different methods to split a tree in a decision tree algorithm?

15598
23:17:23,726 --> 23:17:26,532
So there are three methods to split a decision tree.

15599
23:17:26,958 --> 23:17:28,292
First, we have variance.

15600
23:17:28,974 --> 23:17:33,380
So reduction in variance is an algorithm that is used for continuous target variables.

15601
23:17:33,776 --> 23:17:38,016
This algorithm uses the standard formula of variance to choose the best split.

15602
23:17:38,096 --> 23:17:46,660
So here you can see the standard formula of variance which is summation of x that is all the individual points minus x bar which is the mean

15603
23:17:47,086 --> 23:17:50,052
squared divided by the total number of observations.

15604
23:17:50,798 --> 23:17:55,044
Now the split with lower variance is selected as the criteria to split the population.

15605
23:17:56,622 --> 23:18:06,628
Now the steps to calculate variance is you need to calculate variance for each node and then you need to calculate for each split as the weighted average of each node variance.

15606
23:18:08,174 --> 23:18:12,004
Moving ahead, the second method we have is information gain.

15607
23:18:12,814 --> 23:18:17,284
So information gain is used for splitting the nodes when the target variable is categorical.

15608
23:18:18,638 --> 23:18:20,612
It works on the concept of entropy.

15609
23:18:21,422 --> 23:18:24,740
Now the degree of disorganization in a system is known as entropy.

15610
23:18:25,136 --> 23:18:29,476
So here you can see the formula for information gain which is 1 minus entropy.

15611
23:18:30,606 --> 23:18:33,220
Finally, we have Gini impurity.

15612
23:18:33,774 --> 23:18:43,396
So Gini impurity is the probability of incorrectly classifying a randomly chosen element in the dataset if it were randomly labelled according to the class distribution in the dataset.

15613
23:18:43,616 --> 23:18:46,692
So below you can see the formula for Gini impurity.

15614
23:18:47,216 --> 23:18:58,532
So we have 1 minus summation of PI whole square where n represents the number of classes and P of I represents the probability of randomly picking an element of class I.

