24:10:05,552 --> 24:10:13,792
You might be excited to start building models and diving into algorithms, but before that, you need to understand the core concepts that drive all the machine learning systems.

16133
24:10:14,032 --> 24:10:18,112
These include mathematics, programming, and data handling.

16134
24:10:18,272 --> 24:10:22,112
You don't need to be an expert in all of these areas, but you do need to understand the basics.

16135
24:10:22,286 --> 24:10:25,872
Think of these as building blocks of everything that you will need to learn machine learning.

16136
24:10:26,032 --> 24:10:31,524
Let's start with mathematics. You don't need to be a math genius, but you do need to understand the basics.

16137
24:10:31,792 --> 24:10:38,564
There are three main areas of math that will help you get started out as an ML engineer, and those are linear algebra.

16138
24:10:38,832 --> 24:10:45,312
This is the study of vectors and matrices which are used to manipulate and process data in machine learning models.

16139
24:10:45,472 --> 24:10:51,044
If you've heard terms like feature vectors or matrix operations, that's linear algebra at play.

16140
24:10:51,152 --> 24:10:54,192
This is the core of how machine learning algorithms operate.

16141
24:10:54,432 --> 24:11:04,192
This is the math behind optimizing models. You'll use calculus to adjust the parameters of machine learning models and minimize the error between predicted and the actual values.

16142
24:11:04,352 --> 24:11:09,072
Specifically, derivatives are used to find the best way to fit a model into the data.

16143
24:11:09,312 --> 24:11:10,112
Statistics.

16144
24:11:10,318 --> 24:11:15,312
Machine learning is all about working with uncertainty, and statistics will help you make sense of it.

16145
24:11:15,502 --> 24:11:24,752
Whether you're dealing with probability distributions or hypothesis testing, statistics can help you understand patterns in data and make decisions with uncertain information.

16146
24:11:24,992 --> 24:11:30,432
These mathematical concepts will help you build a more accurate model and optimize it effectively.

