16164
24:12:56,752 --> 24:12:59,072
Let's talk about the different types of machine learning.

16165
24:12:59,232 --> 24:13:05,060
There are three main categories which are supervised learning, unsupervised learning, and reinforcement learning.

16166
24:13:05,392 --> 24:13:13,028
Speaking of supervised learning, this is when you have label data. You train your model on data where the answers are already known.

16167
24:13:13,312 --> 24:13:19,044
The goal is for the model to learn the relationship between inputs and outputs so it can predict the future outcomes.

16168
24:13:19,438 --> 24:13:26,912
Unsupervised learning. In this case, the model works with unlabeled data and it tries to find hidden patterns and groupings in the data.

16169
24:13:27,072 --> 24:13:30,352
This is useful for tasks like clustering or anomaly detection.

16170
24:13:30,670 --> 24:13:31,872
Reinforcement learning.

16171
24:13:32,032 --> 24:13:40,592
This type of learning involves training an agent to make decisions by interacting with its environment and receiving rewards or penalties based on its actions.

16172
24:13:40,752 --> 24:13:43,552
This is often used in game AI or robotics.

16173
24:13:43,792 --> 24:13:49,956
We shall now move on to feature engineering and evaluation. After cleaning your data, the next step is feature engineering.

16174
24:13:50,192 --> 24:13:56,032
This is the process of transforming raw data into meaningful features that help your model make better predictions.

16175
24:13:56,272 --> 24:14:05,764
Once you've engineered your features, it's time to evaluate the model. You'll use metrics like accuracy, precision, and recall to see how well your model is performing.

16176
24:14:06,112 --> 24:14:12,512
Proper evaluation ensures that your model is ready for real world applications and that it can handle data in production.

