In this lesson, we are going to explain the concepts of statistics and probability.

16288
24:24:01,070 --> 24:24:11,108
Describe conditional probability, define the chain rule of probability, discuss the measure of variance, identify the types of Gaussian distribution.

16289
24:24:11,854 --> 24:24:14,308
Basic of statistics and probability.

16290
24:24:15,118 --> 24:24:20,676
Probability and statistics Data Science relies heavily on estimates and predictions.

16291
24:24:21,230 --> 24:24:26,368
A significant portion of data science is made up of evaluations and forecast.

16292
24:24:27,086 --> 24:24:31,364
Statistical methods are used to make estimates for further analysis.

16293
24:24:31,854 --> 24:24:35,140
Probability theory is helpful for making predictions.

16294
24:24:35,534 --> 24:24:43,940
Statistical methods are highly dependent on probability theory, and all probability and statistics are dependent on data.

16295
24:24:44,654 --> 24:24:48,324
Data is information acquired for reference or research

16296
24:24:48,974 --> 24:24:52,164
via observations, facts, and measurements.

16297
24:24:52,750 --> 24:25:00,768
Data is a set of facts structured in the form that computers can interpret, such as numbers, words, estimations,

16298
24:25:00,928 --> 24:25:01,732
and views.

16299
24:25:02,286 --> 24:25:03,488
Importance of data.

16300
24:25:03,822 --> 24:25:10,288
Data aids in seeing more about the information by identifying possible connections between two features.

16301
24:25:10,638 --> 24:25:15,492
Data assists in the detection of distortion by uncovering hidden patterns.

16302
24:25:16,078 --> 24:25:24,288
Based on prior information patterns, data may be utilized to anticipate the future or predict the current state of affairs.

16303
24:25:24,590 --> 24:25:30,980
Also, data aids in determining whether two pieces of information have any instance in common or not.

16304
24:25:31,598 --> 24:25:32,676
Types of data.

16305
24:25:33,134 --> 24:25:34,916
Data might be quantitative.

16306
24:25:35,278 --> 24:25:45,648
That is data that can be measured or counted in numbers, or it may be qualitative, which is data which is generally divided into groups or in simpler words,

16307
24:25:45,888 --> 24:25:48,676
which cannot be counted or measured in numbers.

16308
24:25:49,326 --> 24:25:50,768
Let's consider an example.

16309
24:25:50,990 --> 24:25:56,324
A customer information data of a bank may contain quantitative and qualitative data.

16310
24:25:57,102 --> 24:26:05,888
Consider this snapshot where we have customer ID, surname, geography, gender, age, balance, has seen or card

16311
24:26:06,048 --> 24:26:07,168
is active member.

16312
24:26:07,374 --> 24:26:14,884
Amongst these variables we can see surname is mostly qualitative as it cannot be counted and measured in numbers.

16313
24:26:15,406 --> 24:26:22,448
Geography and gender are also qualitative as they cannot be counted in numbers and are mostly groups.

16314
24:26:22,862 --> 24:26:30,308
Has C or card, that is, has credit card and is active member, although are containing numerical in form.

16315
24:26:30,766 --> 24:26:32,324
But these are categorical.

16316
24:26:32,782 --> 24:26:36,772
That means these have been divided into groups of one and zero

16317
24:26:37,454 --> 24:26:40,260
that represent yes and no as an answer.

16318
24:26:40,910 --> 24:26:44,196
Hence these two variables are also qualitative.

16319
24:26:44,974 --> 24:26:48,772
Customer ID is again, although in numerical data.

16320
24:26:49,070 --> 24:26:54,404
However, the significance or intuition behind customer ID is categorical.

16321
24:26:55,054 --> 24:26:58,400
Hence, it may be kept in the qualitative data also.

16322
24:26:58,990 --> 24:27:01,156
However, age and balance.

16323
24:27:01,614 --> 24:27:08,836
These are numerical information which have been measured or counted and numerical operations can be performed on them.

16324
24:27:09,198 --> 24:27:12,548
Hence, these are under quantitative data categories.

16325
24:27:12,910 --> 24:27:15,588
Introduction to descriptive statistics.

16326
24:27:16,014 --> 24:27:17,520
Descriptive statistics.

16327
24:27:17,870 --> 24:27:25,156
A descriptive measurement is summary measure that quantitatively portrays the most important features of a set of data.

16328
24:27:25,742 --> 24:27:31,332
Allowing for a better comprehension of the information, data can be measured as different levels.

16329
24:27:31,790 --> 24:27:37,764
The levels of measurement describe the nature of information stored in the data assigned to the variables.

16330
24:27:38,222 --> 24:27:41,920
Qualitative data can be measured as nominal or ordinal.

16331
24:27:42,126 --> 24:27:46,692
Quantitative data can be measured in terms of interval and ratio type.

16332
24:27:46,960 --> 24:27:47,920
Nominal data.

16333
24:27:48,142 --> 24:27:52,240
The data is categorized using names, labels, or qualities.

16334
24:27:52,480 --> 24:27:55,680
For example, brand name, zip code, and gender.

16335
24:27:56,014 --> 24:28:00,720
Ordinal data can be arranged in order or ranked and can be compared.

16336
24:28:00,974 --> 24:28:06,564
Examples include grades, star reviews, position and race, and date.

16337
24:28:06,990 --> 24:28:15,760
Interval data is the data that is ordered and has meaningful differences between the data points, example, temperature in Celsius,

16338
24:28:16,000 --> 24:28:17,124
and year of birth.

16339
24:28:17,710 --> 24:28:23,332
Ratio data is similar to the interval level with the added property of inherent zero.

16340
24:28:23,694 --> 24:28:29,092
Mathematical calculations can be performed on both interval as well as ratio data.

16341
24:28:29,710 --> 24:28:32,516
For example, height, age, and weight.

16342
24:28:33,038 --> 24:28:34,820
Population versus sample.

16343
24:28:35,214 --> 24:28:41,060
Before analyzing the data, it's important to figure out if it's from a population or a sample.

16344
24:28:41,550 --> 24:28:47,044
Population is a collection of all available items as well as each unit in our study.

16345
24:28:47,630 --> 24:28:53,220
Sample is a subset of the population that contains only a few units of the population.

16346
24:28:53,838 --> 24:29:00,772
Population data is used for study when the data pool is very small and can give all the required information.

16347
24:29:01,294 --> 24:29:07,940
Samples are collected randomly and represent the entire population in the best possible way.

16348
24:29:08,750 --> 24:29:10,756
Measures of central tendency.

16349
24:29:11,534 --> 24:29:19,204
The central tendency is a single value that aids in the description of the data by determining its center position.

16350
24:29:19,950 --> 24:29:26,532
Measures of central tendency are sometimes known as summary statistics or measures of central location.

16351
24:29:27,342 --> 24:29:32,804
The most popular measurements of central tendency are mean, median, and mode.

16352
24:29:33,518 --> 24:29:41,120
The normal distribution is a bell-shaped, symmetrical distribution in which mean, median, and mode all are equal.

16353
24:29:41,280 --> 24:29:47,236
The curve over here shows the bell-shaped curve or the normal distribution of variable x.

16354
24:29:47,726 --> 24:29:49,840
The point over here that is x1

16355
24:29:50,670 --> 24:29:55,396
is the point which represents the mean median and mode of this distribution.

16356
24:29:55,886 --> 24:29:56,320
Mean.

16357
24:29:56,640 --> 24:30:03,268
Mean is calculated by dividing the sum of all data values by the total number of data values.

16358
24:30:04,014 --> 24:30:07,908
It gets affected when there are unusual or extreme values.

16359
24:30:08,526 --> 24:30:10,532
It is sensitive to the outliers.

16360
24:30:11,200 --> 24:30:18,564
Mean can be calculated as summation over all the values of x in a collection divided by the size of the collection.

16361
24:30:19,502 --> 24:30:26,980
For example, we have a collection where we have values as 7, 3, 4, 1, 6, and 7.

16362
24:30:28,046 --> 24:30:34,244
We find out the sum of these values which is 28, and there are a total of 6 values.

16363
24:30:34,638 --> 24:30:40,000
So 28 divided by 6 gives us a mean value of 4.66.

16364
24:30:40,974 --> 24:30:41,764
Median.

16365
24:30:42,734 --> 24:30:47,460
It is the middle value in the set of the data that has been sorted in ascending order.

16366
24:30:48,494 --> 24:30:54,244
It is a better alternative to mean, since it is less impacted by outliers and skewness.

16367
24:30:55,086 --> 24:30:57,956
It is closer to the actual central value.

16368
24:30:59,054 --> 24:31:02,916
Median is calculated differently for different sizes of data.

16369
24:31:03,950 --> 24:31:07,652
Differentiated as if the total number of values is odd.

16370
24:31:08,480 --> 24:31:11,268
Or if the total number of values is even.

16371
24:31:11,694 --> 24:31:13,860
If the size of the data is odd.

16372
24:31:14,446 --> 24:31:18,660
For example, in this case, we have five elements.

16373
24:31:20,302 --> 24:31:23,396
After sorting, whatever middle value we get.

16374
24:31:24,558 --> 24:31:27,920
That means n plus 1 by tooth term in this case.

16375
24:31:29,742 --> 24:31:31,940
5 plus 1 divided by 2.

16376
24:31:33,166 --> 24:31:37,284
That is the third term, which is 4 is the median value.

16377
24:31:38,574 --> 24:31:44,356
In case when the total number of values is even like here, there are 6 values.

16378
24:31:44,782 --> 24:31:49,504
The average or the mean of the two central values is considered as the median.

16379
24:31:50,062 --> 24:31:54,596
In this case, the median is the mean of 6 and 4, which is 5.

16380
24:31:55,438 --> 24:31:55,984
Mode.

16381
24:31:57,390 --> 24:32:00,772
Mode represents the most common value in the dataset.

16382
24:32:01,710 --> 24:32:05,060
It is not at all affected by extreme observations.

16383
24:32:06,478 --> 24:32:12,420
It is the best measure of central tendency for highly skewed or non-normal distribution.

16384
24:32:13,198 --> 24:32:18,852
Mode for categorical data is determined by estimating the frequencies for each categories,

16385
24:32:19,598 --> 24:32:23,940
and then the category with the highest frequency is considered to be mode.

16386
24:32:25,198 --> 24:32:30,756
Like in this case, 7 has the highest frequency, hence 7 becomes the mode value.

16387
24:32:31,214 --> 24:32:38,564
