16550
24:48:16,462 --> 24:48:20,832
In this module, we will be talking about expectation and variance.

16551
24:48:22,414 --> 24:48:34,500
So the expected value, or we can say mean of a given variable, that we can denote by x is a discrete random variable where it is a weighted average of the possible values that x can take,

16552
24:48:34,672 --> 24:48:40,260
and each value is going to be according to the probability of that specific event occurring.

16553
24:48:41,518 --> 24:48:50,852
So usually the expected value of x is denoted by a simple formula, where we can define the expectation based on the x parameter,

16554
24:48:52,814 --> 24:48:59,140
which is going to be the sum of each possible outcome multiplied by the probability of the outcome occurring.

16555
24:49:01,390 --> 24:49:08,356
So, in more concrete terms, the expectation is what we would expect the outcome of an experiment to be on average.

16556
24:49:11,662 --> 24:49:13,732
We can take an example for the coin.

16557
24:49:14,542 --> 24:49:17,188
If a coin is being tossed 10 times,

16558
24:49:17,966 --> 24:49:21,668
then one is most likely to get 5 heads and 5 tails.

16559
24:49:24,270 --> 24:49:29,252
Same logic can be discussed if we talk about another example of rolling a die.

16560
24:49:29,838 --> 24:49:35,396
So there are 6 possible outcomes when you roll a die, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6.

16561
24:49:35,790 --> 24:49:39,812
And each of these has a probability of 1 by 6 of occurring.

16562
24:49:40,462 --> 24:49:48,624
So we can say that the expectation is going to be 1 multiplied by the probability of that happening, which is going to be 1 by 6

16563
24:49:48,864 --> 24:49:57,024
plus 2 by 6 plus 3 by 6 plus 4 by 6 plus 5 by 6 plus 6 by 6.

16564
24:49:57,198 --> 24:50:00,548
And that is going to give us 3.5 as an output.

16565
24:50:01,038 --> 24:50:03,824
The expected value is 3.5.

16566
24:50:04,590 --> 24:50:10,404
So if you think about it, 3.5 is halfway between the possible values that I can take.

16567
24:50:11,086 --> 24:50:13,156
And this is what we should have expected.

