22124
32:10:31,470 --> 32:10:39,748
Linear equations can be represented in three forms, a standard form, a slope intercept form, or a point slope form.

22125
32:10:41,134 --> 32:10:43,460
Linear equation in standard form.

22126
32:10:43,886 --> 32:10:55,812
A linear equation in standard form for a single variable can be represented as a x plus b equals to zero, where a and b are real integers and x is the variable.

22127
32:10:56,398 --> 32:11:04,624
While a linear equation in standard form for two variable can be represented as ax plus by equals two c

22128
32:11:04,784 --> 32:11:10,372
where ab and c are real integers, while x and y are the variables.

22129
32:11:11,086 --> 32:11:15,172
To summarize a linear equation for variables can be written as

22130
32:11:15,854 --> 32:11:20,836
ax plus by equals to c where x and y are the variables.

22131
32:11:29,838 --> 32:11:32,804
Linear equation in the slope intercept form.

22132
32:11:33,230 --> 32:11:40,260
A linear equation slope can be calculated to see how one variable varies in response to a unit change.

22133
32:11:40,494 --> 32:11:45,904
In another variable, it is represented as y equals to mx plus b,

22134
