where m is the slope, b is the intercept on the y axis and x, and y are the line's distance from the x and the y axis

22135
32:11:56,624 --> 32:11:57,380
respectively.

22136
32:11:59,310 --> 32:12:00,740
Consider this example.

22137
32:12:01,582 --> 32:12:07,844
The lines point at x, y represents the distance from the x and the y-axis respectively,

22138
32:12:11,534 --> 32:12:16,292
while the line intercept on the y-axis is at point zero, b.

22139
32:12:17,774 --> 32:12:19,396
Linear equation slope.

22140
32:12:19,790 --> 32:12:24,324
The slope indicates how steep a line is with respect to y-axis.

22141
32:12:25,038 --> 32:12:29,444
When seen from left to right, it indicates whether the line goes up or down.

22142
32:12:31,054 --> 32:12:37,764
The slope describes how independent variable has been changed, while the dependent variable is changing.

22143
