32:13:35,598 --> 32:13:38,276
Linear equation forms some examples.

22155
32:13:39,214 --> 32:13:47,588
Consider solving the linear equation given as 2x minus 10 divided by 2 equals to 3x minus 1.

22156
32:13:50,574 --> 32:13:52,644
First we will clear the fraction.

22157
32:13:53,838 --> 32:14:00,228
In this example, we can see only left hand side we have 2x minus 10 divided by 2.

22158
32:14:01,134 --> 32:14:04,004
If from the numerator we take 2 as common,

22159
32:14:04,750 --> 32:14:12,560
we will be left with 2 times x minus 5 divided by 2, hence x minus 5 on the left hand side.

22160
32:14:12,782 --> 32:14:17,060
On the right hand side, we still have 3 times x minus 1.

22161
32:14:17,550 --> 32:14:23,972
Now, as a part of next step, we simplify both sides of the equation that has open up the brackets.

22162
32:14:24,430 --> 32:14:31,556
When we do that on the right side, we end up getting 3x minus 3 by multiplying 3 to x minus 1.

22163
32:14:32,430 --> 32:14:37,188
Solving further, we can write as x equals to 3x plus 2.

22164
32:14:37,806 --> 32:14:41,348
Finally, we try to clear the fraction to solve for x.

22165
32:14:42,030 --> 32:14:47,236
We can rearrange the equation as x minus 3x equals to 2.

22166
32:14:48,238 --> 32:14:52,004
Solving it further, we get minus 2x equals to 2.

22167
32:14:53,262 --> 32:14:56,132
And then we solve for x as minus 1.

