25484
36:59:04,880 --> 36:59:15,600
Large language models like ChatGPT 4, Generative Pre-Trained, Transformer 4, O, and Google Gemini are sophisticated AI systems designed to comprehend and generate human-like text.

25485
36:59:15,760 --> 36:59:20,960
These models are built using deep learning techniques and are trained on vast datasets collected from the internet.

25486
36:59:21,262 --> 36:59:29,840
They leverage self-attention mechanisms to analyze the relationship between words or tokens allowing them to capture context and produce coherent relevant responses.

25487
36:59:30,030 --> 36:59:38,960
LLMs have significant applications, including powering virtual assistants, chat boards, content creation, language translation, and supporting research and decision making.

25488
36:59:39,054 --> 36:59:46,480
Their ability to generate fluent and contextually appropriate text has advanced natural language processing and improved human-computer interaction.

25489
36:59:46,606 --> 36:59:49,280
So now let's see what are large language models used for.

25490
36:59:49,550 --> 36:59:55,680
Large language models are utilized in scenarios with limited or no domain specific data available for training.

25491
36:59:55,760 --> 37:00:04,000
These scenarios include both few short and zero short training approaches, which rely on the model's strong inductive bias and its capability to derive meaningful

25492
37:00:04,000 --> 37:00:06,320
representation from a small amount of data.

25493
37:00:06,688 --> 37:00:10,768
Or even no data at all. So now let's see how our large language models are trained.

25494
37:00:11,008 --> 37:00:19,168
Large language models typically undergo pre-training on a board, all encompassing data set that shares statical similarities with the dataset

25495
37:00:19,328 --> 37:00:20,928
specific to the target task.

25496
37:00:21,088 --> 37:00:29,636
The objective of pre-training is to enable the model to require high level features that can later be applied during the fine-tuning phase for specific tasks.

25497
37:00:29,742 --> 37:00:35,888
So there are some training processes of LLM which involves several steps. The first one is text pre-processing.

25498
37:00:35,968 --> 37:00:40,928
The textual data is transformed into a numerical representation that the LLM model can effectively process.

25499
37:00:41,008 --> 37:00:48,288
This conversion may be involved techniques like tokenization and coding and creating input sequences. The second one is random parameter initialization.

25500
37:00:48,398 --> 37:00:53,888
The model's parameters are initialized randomly before the training process begins. The third one is input numerical data.

25501
37:00:54,048 --> 37:00:57,808
The numerical representation of the text data is fed into the model of processing.

25502
37:00:57,968 --> 37:01:05,568
The model's architecture, typically based on transformers, allows it to capture the conceptual relationship between the words or tokens in the next.

25503
37:01:05,648 --> 37:01:13,968
The fourth one is loss function calculation. A loss function calculation measures the discrepancy between the model's prediction and the actual next word or token in a syntax.

25504
37:01:14,128 --> 37:01:17,488
The LLM model aims to minimize this loss during training.

25505
37:01:17,648 --> 37:01:22,608
The fifth one is parameter optimization. The model's parameters are adjusted through optimization technique.

25506
37:01:22,768 --> 37:01:30,128
This involves calculating gradient and updating the parameters accordingly, gradually improving the model's performance. The last one is iterative training.

25507
37:01:30,208 --> 37:01:39,888
The training process is repeated over multiple alterations or epochs until the model's output achieves a satisfactory level of accuracy on that given task or dataset.

25508
37:01:40,048 --> 37:01:46,608
By following this training process, large language models learn to capture linguistic patterns, understand context, and generate coherent responses,

25509
37:01:46,688 --> 37:01:49,860
enabling them to excel at various language-related tasks.

25510
37:01:50,048 --> 37:01:53,248
The next topic is how do large language models work?

25511
37:01:53,454 --> 37:01:59,568
So, large language models leverage deep neural networks to generate output based on patterns learned from the training data.

25512
37:01:59,728 --> 37:02:08,868
Typically, a large language model adopts a transformer architecture which enables the model to identify relationship between words in a sentence irrespective of their position in the sequence.

25513
37:02:09,168 --> 37:02:18,208
In contrast to RNNs that rely on recurrence to capture token relationship, transform a neural network, employ self-attention as their primary mechanism.

25514
37:02:18,382 --> 37:02:25,008
Self-attention calculates attention scores that determine the importance of each token with respect to the other token in the text sequence,

25515
37:02:25,168 --> 37:02:28,688
facilitating the modeling of intricate relationships within the data.

