30756
45:32:38,734 --> 45:32:40,932
First of all, what are the types of clustering?

30757
45:32:41,136 --> 45:32:47,300
There are primarily two categories of clustering hierarchical clustering and then partitional clustering.

30758
45:32:47,694 --> 45:32:56,452
And each of these categories are further subdivided into agglomerative and divisive clustering and k-means and fuzzy C means clustering.

30759
45:32:56,878 --> 45:33:00,644
Let's take a quick look at what each of these types of clustering are.

30760
45:33:01,262 --> 45:33:10,096
In hierarchical clustering, the clusters have a tree like structure, and hierarchical clustering is further divided into agglomerative

30761
45:33:10,336 --> 45:33:11,616
and divisive.

30762
45:33:12,206 --> 45:33:24,176
Agglomerative clustering is a bottom-up approach. We begin with each element as a separate cluster and merge them into successively larger clusters. So for example, we have A, B, C, D, E, F.

30763
45:33:24,496 --> 45:33:33,536
We start by combining B and C form one cluster, D E and E form one more, then we combine D, E, and F one more bigger cluster, and then add B C

30764
45:33:33,776 --> 45:33:35,536
to that, and then finally A to it.

30765
45:33:35,696 --> 45:33:41,056
Compare to that, divisive clustering or divisive clustering is a top down approach.

30766
45:33:41,216 --> 45:33:48,324
We begin with the whole set and proceed to divide it into successively smaller clusters. So we have A, B, C, D, E, F.

30767
45:33:48,416 --> 45:33:51,936
We first take that as a single cluster and then break it down.

30768
45:33:52,384 --> 45:33:54,944
Into A, B, C, D, E, and F.

30769
45:33:55,598 --> 45:34:02,692
Then we have partitional clustering split into two subtypes, k-means clustering and fuzzy c means.

30770
45:34:02,958 --> 45:34:11,984
In k-means clustering, the objects are divided into the number of clusters mentioned by the number k. That's where the k comes from.

30771
45:34:12,144 --> 45:34:18,064
So if we say k is equal to 2, the objects are divided into two clusters, c1 and c2.

30772
45:34:18,464 --> 45:34:27,824
And the way it is done is the features or characteristics are compared and all objects having similar characteristics are clubbed together.

30773
45:34:28,014 --> 45:34:32,704
So that's how k-means clustering is done. We will see it in more detail as we move forward.

30774
45:34:32,784 --> 45:34:40,944
And fuzzy c -means is very similar to k-means in the sense that it clubs objects that have similar characteristics together.

30775
45:34:41,184 --> 45:34:49,424
but while in k-means clustering, two objects cannot belong to or any object. a single object cannot belong to two different clusters.

30776
45:34:49,664 --> 45:34:53,104
in c -means objects can belong to more than one cluster.

30777
45:34:53,264 --> 45:34:57,060
So that is the primary difference between k-means and fuzzy c means.

